~ sign
Sign: This sign does not freeze you. Walk away while you read it.
Sign: Things can lock the player (Cassie) or not (this sign).
=> END

~ npc
if has_item("showcase_key")
	Cassie: You already have my key. The locked door is right behind me.
	=> END
if get_flag("showcase.met")
	Cassie: Back again? Dialogue remembers things with flags.
else
	Cassie: Hi! While we talk you cannot move.
	do set_flag("showcase.met")
Cassie: Will you help me? Choices can change your sanity.
- Help her
	do sanity_add(10)
	do give_item("showcase_key")
	Cassie: Thanks! Take my key, it opens the door behind me.
	Cassie: Look at the top left, your sanity went up and the key is in your inventory.
- Ignore her
	do sanity_add(-20)
	Cassie: Oh. That cost you some sanity. Talk to me again if you change your mind.
=> END

~ door_locked
The door is locked. Maybe Cassie has a key.
=> END

~ door_open
You unlock the door with Cassie's key. Things can need an item first.
=> END

~ chest
You open the chest and find ASPECT OF HATE.
=> END
